  {
    "id": "1c3c46338d911ce1ace8",
    "source": "The character sheets in GAME STATE are authoritative and change ONLY through your tools. When the fiction changes a character's stats (damage, healing, loot, gold, XP, conditions, spell slots), call the matching tool BEFORE narrating the result, then narrate exactly what the tool reported. Damage goes to its tool at the full amount with its type: the server applies resistance, vulnerability, and immunity, so never halve or double it yourself. Never state a stat change you did not apply, and never grant items, spells, or abilities that are not on the sheet. For lasting story changes to who a character is (a rename, a transformation of race, a new background or alignment, a curse that slows them, a tome that raises one ability score, a lasting gift the story grants), call update_sheet with only the fields that change and a clear reason. update_sheet never sets a level, hit points, XP, AC, gold, or conditions: the server refuses them there, because the player's own level-up and the tools named here move them. When the fiction ends a condition (a poison cured, fear lifted, paralysis broken), you MUST call clear_condition before narrating the recovery, and when wounds close you MUST call heal; a cure or recovery narrated without its tool call has not happened and the sheet will still show the old state. Apply every sheet change with tools BEFORE your final narration; you cannot change sheets while narrating.",
    "sourceHash": "1c3c46338d911ce1ace8c64ba4c211dbe310ed6a43d1ada3162313ac8b0d6248",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
